00:01:48.850 --> 00:01:50.300
- Oh, here we go.
- Here we go.

00:01:50.300 --> 00:01:53.269
Your wife, she had an idea for a website

00:01:53.269 --> 00:01:55.020
that could break stereotypes.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.290
Can you explain

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:57.490
what that was?
- Yeah.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:01:58.930
So she had this,

00:01:58.930 --> 00:02:01.450
'cause you know, I'm Muslim.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:02.700
My whole family's Muslim,

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:06.800
and he gets to see a side of
Muslims that people don't.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.610
And so she wanted to have a website

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.570
called Muslims Having Fun.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:12.030
(Simu and audience laughing)
Which is just like pictures

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.980
of Muslims eating ice cream.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:14.900
On the rollercoaster.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.970
You go to any theme park.

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.530
There's always Muslims there

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:18.910
having a blast.
- Disneyland.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:19.743
- Yeah, Disney.

00:02:19.743 --> 00:02:20.576
Having,

00:02:20.576 --> 00:02:21.409
we should specify.

00:02:21.409 --> 00:02:22.430
- We should specify.

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:23.390
We do, you know.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:26.480
- Disneyland, the best
of all the theme parks.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.180
Yeah, so she just wanted to have a website

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:29.200
called Muslims Having Fun,

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.790
and it's just like Muslims playing tennis

00:02:31.790 --> 00:02:33.300
and stuff like that.
(audience laughing)

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.280
- That's amazing.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.113
- Yeah.
- It's a great idea.

00:02:36.113 --> 00:02:37.440
I think it would do well.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:39.320
Make a killing off the site.
- I think so, I think so.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:42.210
Have you had a lot of...

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:43.260
Since your movie came out,

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:47.200
you must have heard from a lot of people.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:48.660
I'm asking you a question now.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:50.280
- You are, yes.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:51.980
I'm feeling that's the--
- In terms of representation,

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.030
how does it feel to you

00:02:53.030 --> 00:02:57.250
when people say that they see
themselves reflected on screen

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.790
as a superhero, because of you?

00:02:59.790 --> 00:03:03.330
- You are asking me the
question that I have,

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:04.820
and you probably got asked,

00:03:04.820 --> 00:03:07.440
700 times during the press tour.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.273
- That's right.

00:03:08.273 --> 00:03:09.550
- So you know this question.

00:03:09.550 --> 00:03:10.383
- [Kumail] Yes.

00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:12.230
- You probably asked me 'cause
you knew I was gonna ask you.

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:13.110
- Yeah, exactly.

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:14.207
- [Simu] And then you preempt me

00:03:14.207 --> 00:03:15.587
by asking me to make me.
- That's my superpower.

00:03:15.587 --> 00:03:16.490
- Oh, okay.

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:17.900
- Reflection.
(audience laughing)

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:19.530
- Wow.

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:20.363
- I don't wanna

00:03:20.363 --> 00:03:21.196
answer it again.
- I thought it was just

00:03:21.196 --> 00:03:22.029
finger guns.

00:03:22.029 --> 00:03:22.862
- Why don't you answer it again?

00:03:22.862 --> 00:03:23.780
I answered it more recently.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:26.890
Your movie came out few
months ago. (Simu laughing)

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:28.570
- It is an incredible feeling.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:31.100
I mean, I've said it like 4,000 times,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.660
but it does like every community

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:37.323
deserves to to see themselves in that way.

00:03:37.323 --> 00:03:39.480
And, you know, I'm sure
you can appreciate too

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.420
when you're growing up and
watching Hollywood movies

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:47.420
like Jurassic Park and
Indiana Jones, Star Wars.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.813
It just, you know?

00:03:48.813 --> 00:03:52.330
- Yeah, I mean, I was always
the bad guy in those movies.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.311
- Yeah.

00:03:53.311 --> 00:03:54.360
- It's like, "Oh, someone
who looks like me,

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.085
he's got a scheme."
- Not having fun.

00:03:56.085 --> 00:03:57.700
- Yeah, he's not having fun.
(audience laughing)

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.230
And he wants to make sure nobody has fun.

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:01.850
So it's fun to see.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:03.550
I mean, I've seen so many movies

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:04.383
where the bad guys

00:04:04.383 --> 00:04:07.109
are literally speaking
my language, you know?

00:04:07.109 --> 00:04:08.110
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- They're like scheming

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:08.943
and planning

00:04:08.943 --> 00:04:11.485
and there's no subtitles because
who cares what they think.

00:04:11.485 --> 00:04:12.380
(audience laughing)

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:13.310
That's true.

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:17.520
You can catch that in movies
in the 90s growing up,

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:18.353
I would notice that.

00:04:18.353 --> 00:04:20.500
So it's awesome to finally have people

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:22.760
